  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to Use Class C4 (HMO-house in multiple occupation) involving single storey infill extension to rear, rear dormer and rear outrigger dormer, with associated amenity, cycle and refuse storage.\r",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, \r\rLocation Plan\rBlock Plan E00\rE01\rE02\rE03\rE04\rP01\rP02\rP03\rP04\rP05\rP06\r\t\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that match the existing building or as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen/dinning/living room on the ground floor shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The rear garden of the site must be accessible and usable at all times by all future occupiers for as long as the property remains in (HMO) use.  \r\rReason: In the interests of the residential amenity and providing a good quality form of accommodation for future residents of the HMO in accordance with the Local Plan.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the 6 long stay cycle parking spaces have been fully constructed in accordance with the approved details and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development. \r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the refuse and recycling storage hereby approved shall be installed in accordance with the approved details and thereafter maintained unless otherwise in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.  \r"
  ],
